.TH FSCK.FILSYS 1 "September 4, 2026" "filsys 1.2.4" "File Format and Disk Utilities"
.SH NAME
fsck.filsys \- filesystem storage and directory consistency check
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fsck.filsys
.RB [ \-v
.IR <v0|v1|v2|v3|v4|v5|v6|v7|32v> ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR block ]
.RB [ \-s ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.I image
.br
.B fsck.filsys
.RB [ \-v
.IR <edition> ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR block ]
.RB { \-N
.IR ino " | " \-C
.IR ino }
.I image
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fsck.filsys
checks a Research Unix filesystem inside a disk image.  It validates the
superblock; walks the i-list building a bit map of every referenced block
(direct and indirect), flagging duplicates and out-of-range blocks; walks the
free-block list against that map, flagging blocks that are both used and free;
reports blocks that are neither used nor free ("missing"); and compares each
inode's link count with the number of directory entries that reference it.
.PP
The Seventh Edition had no single
.I fsck
command: storage consistency was checked with
.BR icheck (8)
(which built a bit map of used blocks and compared it against the free list)
and directory consistency with
.BR dcheck (8)
(which compared each inode's link count with the number of directory entries
that reference it).  The
.I fsck.filsys
name is the modern
.BR fsck (8)
convention, and it folds in the V7 repair toolkit:
.IR icheck ,
.IR dcheck ,
.IR ncheck ,
and
.IR clri ,
plus the Fourth/Fifth Edition
.BR salv (8).
The
.B \-s
option is
.IR icheck 's
.B \-s
free-list rebuild; the
.B \-r
option is
.BR salv (8)
.BR \-a ,
which resolves duplicate blocks by copying each one to a freshly allocated
block and re-pointing the second reference.  The
.B \-N
option is
.BR ncheck (8)
(print an inode's pathname) and
.B \-C
is
.BR clri (8)
(zero an inode);
.B \-n
means "report only, change nothing" (the default, made explicit, and refused
together with the modifying flags).
.PP
The edition is selected with
.BR \-v :
v0 selects the word-addressed PDP-7 filesystem; v1, v2, or v3 select the First
through Third Edition (one format); v4, v5, or v6 select the Sixth Edition
format (V4 and V5 are byte-identical to
V6 on disk); v7 selects Seventh Edition; 32v selects 32V.  The default is v7.  A Research Unix
disk image holds one or more filesystems
.RI ( partitions ),
selected by a partition table compiled into the kernel, not stored on the
disk.  By default
.B fsck.filsys
checks the filesystem at block 0 (the first partition); the
.B \-o
option checks a filesystem at a different block offset.
.PP
The exit status is 0 if the filesystem is clean, 1 if errors were found, and 2
on a usage error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-v " <v0|v1|v2|v3|v4|v5|v6|v7|32v>"
Filesystem edition.  v0 is the word-addressed PDP-7; v1, v2 and v3 are one
format (First through Third Edition); v4, v5 and v6 are byte-identical (the V6
format); v7 is V7; 32v is 32V.
Default v7.  A bare number
.RB ( 0 ,
.BR 1 ,
.BR 4 ,
\&...) is also accepted.
.TP
.BI \-o " block"
Check the filesystem at
.I block
(512-byte blocks) within the image, instead of block 0.
.TP
.B \-s
Rebuild the free list from the block bit map (V7
.IR icheck (8)
.BR \-s ).
This is the standard repair after
.BR restor (8),
which does not rebuild the free list.  Every edition: V7, V6 and PDP-7 rebuild
their free list; V1 rebuilds its free-block map.
.TP
.B \-r
Resolve duplicate blocks: each block referenced by two inodes is copied to a
freshly allocated block and the second reference re-pointed, then the free
list is rebuilt
.RI ( salv (8)
.BR \-a ).
Every edition.
.TP
.B \-n
Report only; change nothing.  This is the default, but makes read-only intent
explicit, and is refused together with
.BR \-s ,
.BR \-r ,
or
.BR \-C .
.TP
.BI \-N " ino"
Print the full pathname(s) of inode
.I ino
.RI ( ncheck (8)).
Every edition.
.TP
.BI \-C " ino"
Zero inode
.I ino
.RI ( clri (8)).
Every edition.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
fsck.filsys image.dk                # check the filesystem at block 0 (V7)
fsck.filsys -v v6 image.dk          # check a V6 (V4/V5) filesystem
fsck.filsys -o 18392 image.dk       # check the filesystem at block 18392
fsck.filsys -s image.dk             # rebuild the free list (icheck -s)
fsck.filsys -r image.dk             # resolve duplicate blocks (salv -a)
fsck.filsys -N 128 image.dk         # print the pathname of inode 128
fsck.filsys -C 128 image.dk         # clear inode 128
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkfs.filsys (1),
.BR findfs.filsys (1),
.BR mount.filsys (1),
.BR filsys (5),
.BR icheck (8),
.BR dcheck (8),
.BR ncheck (8),
.BR clri (8),
.BR salv (8)
